      {
        "id": 79712,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-05T17:10:42.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MarioFanaticXV\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mariofanaticxv/48/2129_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MarioFanaticXV:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Ah… So you can't use Ra's Flesh of the Sun God + Imbued Fire combo to make these cards \"free\" anymore? That's definitely going to set back Ra's usefulness…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not as much as you might think. Solar Flare can still be used as a \"one-shot\" of sorts. If you have Drawn to the Flames in play with the Staff, play Solar Flare, then use DttF to deal all non-hero targets 3 damage at least + 1 more for each villain ongoing. You can still benefit from the card even if you do not keep it in play indefinatly. Ra doesn't need the old super combo to be a damage power house. He still does that better than most.&nbsp;</p>",
